Simplified clab topology to test SRv6 uSID use case for AI workloads. Note that in "real life", this will require a dedicated controller and for the GPU NICs to be a tunnel endpoint.

Simple Test, from host1:
ping srv6 sid fc00:1:333:: via segment-list fc00:1:101:11:103:: source lo100

Evaluate SRv6 removing segment-list hops along the way with tcpdump:
bash tcpdump -i <interface> -vvvnn

Eventually you should see the final payload of 2001:db8:1::21 > fc00:1:333:: when it reaches host3.
